## ✍ DM Response
As Dorian Ashgrove leads the party towards the Aldwick Mine entrance, the chill of the marsh air settles around them like a spectral shroud. The iron doors loom before you, stamped with intricate runes that seem to dance in the flickering light of his lantern. The lantern's glow reveals Father Vane's possession still lingers over Ravenmoor, casting an uneasy pall over the village.

Dorian compares the runes from his transcription against those on the doors, searching for any patterns or sequences that might hold a clue. His expert eye scans the marks carefully, his mind racing with possibilities and theories. The air seems to grow colder as he works, the silence of the night pressuring him to make sense of what he sees.

After several tense moments, Dorian's gaze settles on a sequence that catches his attention. He takes a deep breath, his hands trembling slightly as he confirms his findings with Emmett Grave. The graverobber turns over the third language transcription, confirming the match.

The runes spell out "Awakening," and Dorian knows this cannot be good news. As the group debates their next move, they feel a sudden shiver of unease — a sensation that something is watching them from the darkness beyond the mine entrance. The cold wind picks up, whispering strange words and secrets through the trees, as if sharing with them the horrors that lay hidden within the depths of the Aldwick Mine.

As the party prepares to enter the mine, they cannot shake the feeling that their actions may have awakened something far darker than they had imagined. The malevolent force that possessed Father Vane seems to be growing stronger, its influence spreading throughout Ravenmoor like a malignant shadow.

The party has no choice but to press forward, armed with the knowledge that they may have set in motion events beyond their control. As they step into the mine entrance, they cannot help but feel the weight of their decision bearing down upon them, the darkness of the mine seeming to echo the darkness growing within Ravenmoor itself.

The Aldwick Mine swallows them whole, leaving behind only the faintest trace of lantern light to mark their passing into the unknown. The shadows of the mine stretch out before them like a labyrinthine maze, filled with twists and turns that seem designed to confuse and disorient.

As they venture deeper into the mine, they begin to feel a palpable sense of dread growing within them — as if they are being watched by unseen eyes, their every move tracked by some malevolent force lurking in the darkness. The air grows colder still, a chill that seems to seep into their bones and fill them with an icy fear.

The party presses onward, determined to uncover the secrets hidden within the mine and put an end to the darkness that has befallen Ravenmoor. But as they delve deeper into the heart of the mine, they cannot escape the feeling that they are being led further and further away from the light — and closer and closer to the abyss.

## 📋 Summary
Dorian Ashgrove matched the runes on the Aldwick Mine doors with his transcription, discovering they spell out "Awakening." Unsettled by the revelation and a feeling of being watched, the party ventured into the mine, bracing for the awakened malevolent force that might have been stirred.
